# Affiliate Intake — credentials & environment
# ---------------------------------------------
# This workflow needs NO credentials and NO environment variables.
#
# All 13 nodes are Code / IF / Merge / Manual Trigger / Sticky Note —
# workflow.json contains zero credential blocks, zero $env references and
# zero external API calls. This file exists only to complete the
# per-workflow folder contract; there is intentionally nothing to set below.
#
# Demo = the whole workflow, as shipped:
#   Import workflow.json → click "Test workflow". Done.
#
# Going live (optional, your own build — not part of this export):
#   - Replace "Demo intake: sample applications" with a real intake
#     trigger (n8n Form Trigger, or a Tally/Typeform webhook) emitting the
#     same item shape (see examples/affiliate-intake/test-data.json).
#   - Add a delivery node — e.g. Gmail (Gmail OAuth2 credential) or Slack
#     (Slack OAuth2 / bot token credential) — after "Draft outreach",
#     "Owner alert" and "Owner digest".
#   Any such credentials live in n8n's credential store, not in this file.
#
# (intentionally empty — no values required)
